"type":"photo","url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUN84quXUAExAmH.jpg","width":1080},{"alt_text":"A young star cluster filled with many stars that display Webb’s unique eight-pronged diffraction pattern. At its center is a yellow star which sports the largest diffraction pattern. To the left of the star, there is a region filled with yellow dust and gas. This yellow region extends from the bottom, covering about two-thirds of the image. The yellow region has several blue stars of different sizes embedded within. The top third, which lies outside of the yellow region, holds a few bright protostars, within dense gray gas. Those stars illuminate the gas, making it appear blue. A few red outflows from other protostars are visible above this grayish-blue region. To the right of the central star, there is a clumpy, flame-like plume of red dust and gas with protostars that emit a soft white light within. The plume is surrounded by more dense gray gas and dust.","height":1911,"media_key":"3_2108662422462480384","type":"photo","url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUN5TRIXQAAuu31.jpg","width":2048},{"height":321,"media_key":"3_2108659866118365184","type":"photo","url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUN2-eAboAA_2aj.jpg","width":1080},{"height":900,"media_key":"3_2108658180372762624","type":"photo","url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUN1cWHXEAAc4Da.jpg","width":992},{"duration_ms":16068,"height":1280,"media_key":"13_2108324320271282176","preview_image_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2108324320271282176/img/1XwN8KhdU7loyMZm.jpg","type":"video","width":720},{"height":600,"media_key":"3_2108651653721436160","type":"photo","url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUNvgccbMAAhVS7.jpg","width":1080},{"duration_ms":44511,"height":1920,"media_key":"13_2108273049225113600","preview_image_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2108273049225113600/img/uFUwRYVtm3dbA7yb.jpg","type":"video","width":1080},{"alt_text":"The four members of Crew-12 posed inside the \"door\" leadin